invariant: INV-26
file: aes.c
catches: aes_runtime_test
reason: a QUIC host object runs every block of a schedule the table
  expanded on the AES instructions, so a session whose caller did not set
  CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_AES executes AES instructions on its Initial
  packets and dies of SIGILL on a CPU without them. The bytes do not
  change, because both ciphers keep one round-key layout, so no vector
  notices. bin/aes_runtime_test counts the calls into aes_hw.c without
  the bit and requires none.

--- old
    return s->instructions == AES_ON_INSTRUCTIONS;
--- new
    return s->instructions != 0;
